MintVID libmpeg2 import
========================

This directory contains the portable decoding core from VideoLAN libmpeg2
0.5.1. MintVID builds only the generic C allocation, parser, IDCT, motion
compensation and slice sources. Unix frontends, output plugins and
architecture-specific assembly are intentionally omitted.

Upstream: https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libmpeg2
License: GNU GPL version 2 or later; see COPYING and the source headers.

config.h is MintVID-specific. It selects portable C and declares the Amiga
m68k target big-endian for both GCC and vbcc builds.

MintVID changes to the imported sources
---------------------------------------

Both produce output bit-identical to the imported C code.

- libmpeg2/motion_comp_swar.c (new): motion compensation working on four
  pixels per 32-bit word. The four-way half-pel average uses the byte
  split from RiVA's MacrosInterpol68k.m (Henryk Richter, GPL-2.0-or-later).
  mpeg2_mc_init() selects it (mpeg2_mc_swar) instead of mpeg2_mc_c, which
  stays compiled as the reference for tests/mr_mpeg2_mc_check.c.
- libmpeg2/idct.c: mpeg2_idct_copy_c/mpeg2_idct_add_c skip all-zero rows
  and use reduced column passes when only storage row 0, or rows 0 and 4,
  are non-zero. tests/mr_mpeg2_idct_check.c compares them against the
  imported code, kept in tests/mr_mpeg2_idct_reference.h.
